# The GPU stops taking work in a run: from the control port's gpustall on, every GPU submission vanishes, neither run nor reported, as in the driver
# that stopped taking a Mac's submissions on 2026-11-08 (the game then waited on its fence for ever). The GPU watchdog takes the GPU as lost after
# DM_GPU_LOST_S, nothing waits for it any more, the game saves and quits by itself, and the note for the next launch is written (nvn_mtl.m gpu_watch,
# front.h front_gpu_lost). DM_TEST_GPU_LOST_NOTE also starts the run as if the last session had ended so: the note is taken (and told on a window)
# The hang recorder prints its record twice: after 2 s with work waiting (DM_HANGREC_EARLY_S) and when the GPU is taken as lost; the vanished
# submissions were never run, so none of their passes finished
name gpu_lost
requires cli mac-app
save warlock
timeout 180
env DM_GPU_LOST_S=3 DM_TEST_GPU_LOST_NOTE=1

enter_game
stick 0 1 frames=30
fault arm gpustall
expect gpu_lost timeout=30
expect quit_save timeout=30
check event fault point=gpustall
check event quit_save saved=true
check exit 0
check saved
check log_has "the last session ended when the GPU stopped responding \(saved 1\)"
check log_has "a note for the next launch says the GPU stopped responding \(written\)"
check log_has "\[hang\] no GPU work has finished for [0-9.]+ s with work waiting"
check log_has "\[hang\] the GPU is taken as lost"
check log_has "\[hang\] submission [0-9]+ \(frame [0-9]+\): 0 of its [0-9]+ passes finished"
check log_has "\[hang\] scene: area [0-9]+ at"
check no_red_log "allow=GPU lost|the GPU stopped responding"
